# Agent model routing (v1)

This rule **assigns models**. It does not replace `.cursor/rules/01`–`07` or `AGENTS.md`. Authoritative workflow: `.cursor/rules/development-workflow.mdc`. Branch/PR/no-merge: rule `10`. Do not weaken tenant isolation, the permission matrix, `PERMISSION_ENFORCEMENT`, `MULTITENANT_ENFORCEMENT`, honesty tagging, or scope control. Never log or commit API keys, vault payloads, or credential dumps.

Choose the **best available model** for the coding and review stages. Cursor catalog IDs below are v1 pins. They are Cursor-hosted models, not independently configured OpenAI/Anthropic/Google keys. Do not assume Codex or Cursor Auto/Router unless the current spawn catalog lists them.

## v1 default pins

| role | model | absolute |
|---|---|---|
| coding agent (default) | composer-2.5 | no |
| ai-llm work | cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast | yes |
| security review | claude-opus-5-thinking-high | yes |
| Security/QA review (default) | gpt-5.6-sol-high | yes |

`composer-2.5` is the **normal implementation model**. It **must not be an absolute assignment**.

Optional specialist definitions in `.cursor/agents/` retain their frontmatter pins when invoked for focused review.

## Complexity/risk escalation

The coding agent **may** escalate to a stronger available model when the task involves any of:

- complex architecture or refactoring
- difficult debugging
- high-risk financial/business logic
- complex database migrations or data integrity
- concurrency or performance-sensitive backend work
- complex third-party API/OAuth behavior
- unusually large cross-domain implementation

Complex OAuth still requires a **Security** review pass. Record the trigger in `ESCALATION REASON`. Do not default `composer-2.5-fast` or Opus Fast.

### Stronger-model ladder (implementers)

Use the first slug available in the current spawn catalog:

1. `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`
2. `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high`
3. `gpt-5.6-sol-high`
4. `inherit`

## Review-pass independence

- **Security/QA review** should use a different provider family from the implementer when a separate reviewer is available. Default review model is OpenAI `gpt-5.6-sol-high`. If the implementer already used GPT-5.6, fall back to `gemini-3.7-flash-high` then `gpt-5.6-luna-high`.
- For auth/permissions/tenant/credentials/OAuth/encryption changes, prefer Anthropic `claude-opus-5-thinking-high` for the security portion of the review.
- If no separate reviewer is available, perform an explicit review pass and **disclose that it was not independent** (development-workflow.mdc).
- Built-in Explore/Bash/Browser keep Cursor’s automatic faster-model selection. Do not pin `auto` / `auto-smart` in `.cursor/agents/*.md`.

## Stage recording

Record `MODEL`, `MODEL SOURCE`, and `ESCALATION REASON` for implementation and review stages in the PR body. `MODEL SOURCE` is one of: `frontmatter`, `lead-override`, `inherit`, `cursor-fallback`.

Never write secrets into `MODEL`, `REASON`, or logs.

## Fallbacks when a preferred model is unavailable

Plan, admin, or catalog gaps: use the same-family sibling, then `inherit`, then `composer-2.5` as the Cursor-pool floor. If Cursor ignores a pin, record `MODEL SOURCE: cursor-fallback`.

## Forbidden

- Merging PRs or enabling auto-merge
- Pinning Codex or Cursor Auto/Router in agent frontmatter unless those IDs are verified in the current catalog
- Defaulting Claude Fable 5 (privacy/retention and cost)
- Treating Composer 2.5 as un-escalatable for routine implementation
